<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Susa, Piedmont</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Segusio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> is a town in the Susa valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, at the foot of the routes over the Montgenèvre and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mont-cenis">Mont Cenis</a> passes. As Segusio it was the seat of the Alpine kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnus">Donnus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-julius-cottius">Cottius</a> and later of the small Roman province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cottian-alps">Cottian Alps</a>. It keeps an Arch of Augustus, a Roman amphitheatre and medieval churches.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/susa-piedmont.jpg" alt="Susa, Piedmont" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pippo-b · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Susa_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
